.\" gpu-mock - the GPU mock: the device nodes, the fake pciconf, devinfo and
.\" sysctl answers, and the RM escape ioctls, all made of one model file.
.\"
.Dd November 26, 2026
.Dt GPU-MOCK 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm gpu-mock
.Nd the GPU mock of the NVIDIA FreeBSD driver
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm gpu-mock
.Nm daemon
.Op Ar model
.Nm gpu-mock
.Nm pciconf
.Op Fl l | lv | lvb
.Op Ar model
.Nm gpu-mock
.Nm devinfo
.Op Ar selector
.Op Ar model
.Nm gpu-mock
.Nm sysctl
.Ar name
.Op Ar model
.Nm gpu-mock
.Nm decide
.Op Ar model
.Nm gpu-mock
.Nm nodes
.Op Ar model
.Nm gpu-mock
.Nm model
.Op Ar model
.Nm gpu-mock
.Fl -help
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The GPU mock is a device, a set of answers and a set of ioctls that stand
for an NVIDIA card without one.
.Pp
It has three parts and no kernel module:
.Bl -tag -width "the seam" -compact
.It the model
One JSON file per card, in the schema
.Pa gpu-model.v1 :
the cards of one box, the provider that claims them, the generation each
card belongs to, the firmware that generation needs and the faults the model
scripts.
.It the seam
The fake
.Xr pciconf 8 ,
.Xr devinfo 8
and
.Xr sysctl 8
answers, made of the same model.
.It the RM engine
The RM escape ioctls of
.Xr libnvrm 3 ,
answered from the same model.
.El
.Pp
The daemon publishes the nodes the real driver publishes,
.Pa /dev/nvidiactl ,
one node per card of the model,
.Pa /dev/nvidia_modeset
and
.Pa /dev/nvidia_uvm ,
with
.Xr cuse 3 ,
so a jail that is given the nodes sees what a client of the driver sees.
The two last nodes carry an underscore where the driver has a dash: the
mechanism of
.Xr cuse 3
replaces a character it does not know in a device name with an underscore.
The nodes go away with the daemon: it destroys them before it leaves.
The environment variable
.Ev GPU_MOCK_PREFIX
names the nodes instead, for a host where the driver's names are taken or
for two mocks side by side.
.Pp
Every answer of the mock is a mock.
It never counts as a hardware result, and every answer says so.
.Sh THE SWITCH
.Sy scripts/gpu-mock-up.sh
is the one switch: it starts the daemon, it writes the ruleset of the nodes
and it prints the environment of the seam.
.Bd -literal -offset indent
sh scripts/gpu-mock-up.sh up rtx5060ti
sh scripts/gpu-mock-up.sh down
.Ed
.Pp
The model is the value of
.Ev GPU_MOCK ,
else the argument.
.Cm down
stops the mock with the names of
.Ev GPU_MOCK_PREFIX ,
so the prefix of the mock that runs is the one it is given.
The switch needs the right to open
.Pa /dev/cuse
and the right to change the rules of the kernel: it runs the daemon and the
rules through
.Xr doas 1
or
.Xr sudo 8
when this user is not root, and it says so when neither is set up.
.Pp
The switch puts the rules of the nodes in force before the daemon makes
the nodes, so the nodes are created with the mode and the group of the
rules.
The rules it puts in force are taken away by
.Cm down ,
the nodes and the rules with them.
.Pp
The ruleset of the nodes is a fragment of
.Pa /etc/devfs.rules :
the ruleset is named
.Ql gpumock
and its number is 63.
A jail takes the rules with
.Ql devfs_ruleset=63
in its
.Xr jail 8
parameters, and the nodes themselves are given to the jail by binding them
into it.
The machine of the operator takes the rules at boot with
.Ql devfs_system_ruleset="gpumock"
in
.Pa rc.conf .
.Sh THE MODEL
A model file names its schema, the model, the driver version, the providers,
the bases, the boards, the cards and the faults.
A base is a generation: its architecture, its implementation, its SM count,
its class list and its page sizes.
A board is a decorator over a base: it adds or overrides, and never decides.
A card is a board at a PCI address, with the identity the RM gives it.
.Pp
A model file may name other model files in its
.Pa include
member; the box of a mixed machine is made of the cards of one file each.
The provider, the base and the board of an included file are taken once, by
name.
.Pp
The files of the repository are in
.Pa data/models :
one JSON per card, the provider record they share, a box that composes
them, and two models that script a fault.
.Sh THE SEAM
The seam answers the hardware of the operating system layer:
the
.Xr pciconf 8
and
.Xr devinfo 8
output, and the
.Pa hw.nvidia *
and
.Pa dev.nvidia *
system controls.
.Pp
The answers of the seam come from the model.
The
.Xr pciconf 8
and
.Xr devinfo 8
answers open with a marker line that no real tool prints, and the version
banner of the mock says
.Dq GPU MOCK .
.Pp
The seam shim is the seam for a program that reads the hardware through the
system calls:
.Xr libnvrm 3
and
.Xr nvrm-info 8
read the model when the shim is loaded.
It answers the system controls of the model and the RM escape ioctls in the
program's own process, so a CI run needs no device and no right.
.Sh THE FAULTS
A model scripts the faults it wants:
.Bl -tag -width "device_lost" -compact
.It device_lost
The card is gone: the RM does not list it, and the controls that need it
answer that the object is not found.
.It alloc_refused
Every allocation is refused with
.Dv NV_ERR_INSUFFICIENT_RESOURCES .
.It ioctl_failed
The call itself fails.
.El
.Sh THE COMMANDS
.Bl -tag -width "gpu-mock model" -compact
.It Nm daemon
Op Ar model
Publish the nodes of the model and serve them.
Needs the
.Xr cuse 3
module and the right to open
.Pa /dev/cuse .
.It Nm pciconf
Op Fl l | lv | lvb
Op Ar model
The mock's
.Xr pciconf 8
answer.
The flags are the ones of
.Xr pciconf 8 .
.It Nm devinfo
Op Ar selector
Op Ar model
The mock's
.Xr devinfo 8
answer.
.It Nm sysctl
.Ar name
Op Ar model
The mock's
.Xr sysctl 8
answer.
.It Nm decide
Op Ar model
The decision on every card of the model: whether a provider claims it,
whether its generation is above the floor of the provider, and whether the
firmware of that generation is built.
.It Nm nodes
Op Ar model
The
.Xr devfs.rules 5
ruleset of the nodes of the model, the rules a jail that runs the mock's
clients needs.
.It Nm model
Op Ar model
The model as one JSON document.
.El
.Sh ENVIRONMENT
.Bl -tag -width "GPU_MOCK_DIR" -compact
.It Ev GPU_MOCK
The model: a file, or a name under the model directory.
Every command that takes a model uses it when no model is given.
.It Ev GPU_MOCK_DIR
The directory of the model files.
The default is
.Pa /usr/local/share/nvidia-gb10-freebsd/models ;
a mock that is run from a checkout finds the models of the checkout
(
.Pa data/models )
when the installed directory holds no model of that name.
.It Ev GPU_MOCK_PREFIX
The names of the nodes the daemon publishes.
The default is
.Dq nvidia ,
so the nodes are the ones the driver publishes.
Name them when those names are taken, or when two mocks live side by side.
.It Ev GPU_MOCK_PIDFILE
The file the daemon writes its own line in.
The default is
.Pa /var/run/gpu-mock.pid ;
the file holds a line for every mock that runs on this machine.
.El
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width ".Pa" -compact
.It Pa data/models
The model files: one JSON per card, the provider record they share, a box
that composes them and two models that script a fault.
.It Pa schema/gpu-model-1.schema.json
The schema of a model file.
.It Pa schema/gpu-mock-1.schema.json
The schema of the document of the
.Nm model
command.
.It Pa /var/run/gpu-mock.pid
The registry of the mocks that run on this machine: every line is a pid, the
names of the nodes of that mock and the token of the run that started it.
.It Pa /var/run/gpu-mock-nvidia.rules
The ruleset of the nodes that the switch writes: a fragment of
.Pa /etc/devfs.rules .
The name carries the names of the nodes, so two mocks side by side do not
write over each other.
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Nm gpu-mock
exits 0 when the command succeeded, 1 when it failed, and 2 when the
arguments were wrong.
.Sh EXAMPLES
The decision on the card of a model:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
gpu-mock decide rtx5060ti
.Ed
.Pp
The answers of the seam for a CI run:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
export GPU_MOCK=rtx5060ti
export GPU_MOCK_DIR=data/models
export LD_PRELOAD=src/gb10-gpu-mock/build/libgpubmockshim.so
nvrm-info --json
.Ed
.Pp
The nodes of the model, and the rules that give them to a jail:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
gpu-mock nodes rtx5060ti
.Ed
.Pp
The one switch: the daemon, the rules of the nodes and the seam:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
sh scripts/gpu-mock-up.sh up rtx5060ti
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr cuse 3 ,
.Xr libnvrm 3 ,
.Xr devfs.rules 5 ,
.Xr nvrm-info 8 ,
.Xr pciconf 8 ,
.Xr sysctl 8
.Sh CAVEATS
The CUSE mechanism copies the argument of an ioctl into the window it shares
with the daemon, and the pointers inside that argument name the address
space of the client.
CUSE cannot carry them.
The ioctls of the RM whose argument holds such a pointer, the card list and
the control parameters among them, are therefore refused over a node with
.Er EINVAL ,
and the daemon says why.
The seam shim answers them in the client's own process, where the pointers
are the client's own.
.Pp
The name of a node that CUSE creates holds no dash:
the daemon publishes
.Pa /dev/nvidia_modeset
and
.Pa /dev/nvidia_uvm ,
where the driver publishes
.Pa /dev/nvidia-modeset
and
.Pa /dev/nvidia-uvm .
The ruleset of the nodes names the nodes that exist, so a rule of the
ruleset matches them.
.Pp
Over a node the errno of the engine reaches the client in the CUSE error
that carries it:
.Er EINVAL ,
.Er ENOMEM
and
.Er EFAULT
keep their meaning.
The mechanism has no
.Er ENOTTY ,
so a command the RM does not know reaches the client as
.Er ENXIO .
.Pp
The nodes of a daemon that was killed stay in the kernel:
the mechanism does not take them away by itself.
The daemon destroys them when it is stopped, but a daemon that was killed
leaves its names behind, and they cannot be freed without a reboot.
Use
.Ev GPU_MOCK_PREFIX
on such a host.
